+## D115 — One indexed shader cache file, prepared before the game draws (2026-11-07, Mad Riders)
+
+**Decision:** the pipeline storage (D42) and the driver's pipeline cache (D45) become one file, by default
+`<cache root>/native_x_renderer/<title id>.cache`, or where the game puts it with `SetShaderCache` (Mad Riders:
+`shaders.cache` next to the exe). It holds an index (kind, type, hash, modification → offset, size) over 16-byte
+aligned blobs: guest microcode, the translator's SPIR-V of every translation, pipeline records, the driver's cache.
+What is new in a run is appended as a journal and folded into the index when the file is written whole (to a
+temporary, renamed over it). At each start, before the game's first command, the renderer prepares all of it while the
+game waits: microcode analyzed, host shaders made from the stored SPIR-V (no translation), every pipeline created and
+compiled; the window shows the game's ImGui dialogs meanwhile (its status screen, `GetShaderCacheStatus`), and every
+core but one works on the translation queue. A game can hand over every shader it ships (fingerprint + scan): the
+first start then analyzes them all and translates its pixel shaders for each interpolator set its vertex shaders
+write, with the depth modes its alpha test may need. Stored SPIR-V of another render scale or SPIR-V version is
+dropped and made again.
+
+**Why:** Mad Riders: objects appeared late the first time each was seen in a run, the stored pipelines were created
+after the first draw at 64 per frame, and the cache was three files in the user's cache folder. Stored SPIR-V spares
+the translator (up to 2.7 ms a shader) on every later start.
+
+**How to use and extend it:** [`shader-cache.md`](shader-cache.md).
+
+**Limits:** vertex shaders reach the GPU with their vertex fetches patched by the game's D3D for each vertex layout,
+so the shipped microcode cannot be translated ahead; their variants are kept as the game uses them. The pixel
+translations are guesses (no MSAA centroids, no PsParamGen); what draws ask that was not guessed is translated as
+before and kept.
